Build the ntfy client for GOOS=wasip1 and reach slicc-kernel for HTTP and commands.

Reason: ntfy v2.32.0's client (-tags noserver) does not build for wasip1:
cmd/subscribe_unix.go and cmd/publish_unix.go omit wasip1, so
scriptLauncher, processExists and the help suffix are undefined, and
client/config_unix.go leaves the default config path empty. wasip1 also
cannot dial or spawn. slicchost talks to host/ntfy-host.mjs (ntfy_host
probe/call/take): http.DefaultTransport (what client.Client uses) sends
requests there and reads the body chunk by chunk, yielding to other
goroutines before each blocking read, so ntfy sub runs a message's command
as soon as the line arrives. ntfy sub's per-message command runs as
sh -c <command> through the host's spawn (no temp script, which wasip1
would create 0644 and could not exec), with the NTFY_* environment and the
process stdio inherited, one message at a time as upstream. pub --wait-cmd
runs its command the same way. pub --wait-pid fails with a clear error:
there is no process table to watch. The config file is
~/.config/ntfy/client.yml ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ntfy/client.yml when set).

Upstream: not filed (homescoop does not file upstream reports).
removeWhen: ntfy's client builds for GOOS=wasip1 and wasip1 can dial and
spawn, without this patch.

